## A Surge in Recalls

With 759 recalls already marked for 2026, we're nearing an all-time record. Class I recalls, the most severe, lead the pack with 206 incidents, and common causes include salmonella and undeclared allergens. June alone contributed a staggering 213 recalls.

## Corporate Repeat Offenders

Brands like Spring & Mulberry Inc., Moonlight Packing Corporation, and Ghirardelli Chocolate Company earned a spot on our watchlist. Particularly egregious, Spring & Mulberry Inc. faced 11 Class I recalls this year due to potential salmonella contamination in their products.

## Recent Highlights

This month's recalls are a mix of the familiar and the unsettling:

- **Joy Gourmet Foods LLC** failed to pasteurize their lassi products properly, resulting in a Class II recall.
- **Spring & Mulberry Inc.** struggles with salmonella, yet again, in their chocolate products.
- **Utz Quality Foods, LLC** recalls chips due to suspected salmonella contamination.

## Conclusion

The persistent occurrence of food recalls serves as a bitter reminder of the need for stringent quality control and accountability. While progress is evident, the high number of repeat offenders indicates a lack of incentive or ability to rectify systemic issues. Consumer vigilance remains a crucial counterbalance.
